4. Hybrid Feasible Domain in the (v,g) Plane

4.1 Three Boundaries

Because the active force participates in the vertical balance, three distinct boundaries exist:

Physical PMEDS boundary:

\boxed{
v_{\rm phys}(g)
=
\inf\{v:
F_M(v,g)\ge mg\}
}

Hybrid support boundary:

\boxed{
v_{\rm hybrid}(g)
=
\inf\{v:
F_M(v,g)+F_{\rm active,max}^{+}\ge mg\}
}

Magnetic-dominant boundary:

\boxed{
v_{\rm magnetic}(g)
=
\inf\{v:
F_M(v,g)\ge mg-F_{W,\min}\}
}

4.2 Hybrid Feasible Domain

\boxed{
\mathcal D_H=
\left\{
(v,g):
\begin{aligned}
&g_{\min}\le g\le g_{\max},\\
&F_M(v,g)+F_{\rm active,max}^{+}\ge mg,\\
&P_D(v,g)\le P_{\max}
\end{aligned}
\right\}
}

For a nominal active force value F_{\rm active}^{\rm nom}, replace F_{\rm active,max}^{+} with F_{\rm active}^{\rm nom}.

4.3 Power Boundary

The power boundary v_{\rm power}(g) solves:

P_D(v,g)=P_{\max}

If P_D^\infty(g)\le P_{\max}, the constraint is inactive.

4.4 Existence

Proposition 4.1. \mathcal D_H\neq\varnothing iff there exists g\in[g_{\min},g_{\max}] with:

F_\infty(g)+F_{\rm active,max}^{+}>mg

and

P_D(v_{\rm power},g)\le P_{\max}

for some v_{\rm power}.

Proof. Necessity: the lift constraint requires F_\infty+F_{\rm active,max}^{+}>mg; else no v satisfies the hybrid support condition. Sufficiency: take any such g, choose v=\max(v_{\rm hybrid}(g),v_{\rm power}(g)). ∎

4.5 Numerical Example

With reference parameters:

F_\infty(0.020)\approx 8718\,{\rm N},\qquad \frac{F_\infty}{mg}\approx 1.777

v_{\rm phys}(0.020)=\frac{1.6}{\sqrt{1.777-1}}\approx 1.82\,{\rm m/s}\approx 6.5\,{\rm km/h}

At v=5 m/s: F_M\approx 7910 N \approx 1.61\,mg.

Power at v=8 m/s:

P_D(8)=8718\times 1.6\times\frac{64}{64+2.56}\approx 13.4\,{\rm kW}

