5. Power Budget

5.1 Levitation Drag Power

P_D(v,g)=F_\infty(g)\frac{v_t}{1+(v_t/v)^2}

Saturates at P_D^\infty=F_\infty v_t\approx 13.95 kW.

5.2 Propulsion Power

P_{\rm prop}(v)=v\left(F_{\rm aero}(v)+F_{\rm roll}+F_{D}^{\rm residual}(v)\right)

For a 500 kg vehicle at v=8 m/s with C_dA\approx 0.7 m²:

F_{\rm aero}=\frac12\rho C_dA v^2\approx 0.5\times 1.225\times 0.7\times 64\approx 27\,{\rm N}

F_{\rm roll}\approx 0.01\,mg\approx 49\,{\rm N}

P_{\rm prop}(8)\approx 8\times(27+49)\approx 610\,{\rm W}

5.3 Total Power

P_{\rm total}=P_D+P_{\rm prop}+P_{\rm ctrl}

At v=8 m/s with the reference parameters:

P_{\rm total}\approx 13.4+0.6+2\approx 16\,{\rm kW}

Below the provisional 20 kW system-level design budget under the reduced-order model. This leaves approximately 4 kW of margin, which must absorb P_{\rm ctrl}+P_{\rm conversion}+P_{\rm thermal}+P_{\rm sensing}+P_{\rm active} and additional guidance system losses.

5.4 Regenerative Braking

The magnetic energy dissipated over a deceleration interval [t_0,t_1] is:

E_{\rm mag}=\int_{t_0}^{t_1}P_D(t)\,dt

The recoverable energy is:

\boxed{
E_{\rm rec}=
\eta_{\rm reg}
\int_{t_0}^{t_1}
P_D(t)\,dt
}

with \eta_{\rm reg}\in[0,1] the recovery efficiency.

