6. Safety Envelope

6.1 Combined Safe Set

\boxed{
\mathcal{K}=\mathcal{K}_{\rm gap}\cap\mathcal{K}_{\rm wheel}\cap\mathcal{K}_{\rm velocity}\cap\mathcal{K}_{\rm actuator}\cap\mathcal{K}_{\rm drag}\cap\mathcal{K}_{\lambda}
}

· Gap: g_{\min}\le g_i\le g_{\max}
· Wheel: F_{W,i}\ge F_{W,\min}
· Velocity: v\ge v_{\rm rob} when \lambda\to 1
· Actuator: F_{\rm active}\in[-F_{\rm active,max}^{-},F_{\rm active,max}^{+}]
· Drag: P_D(v,g)\le P_{\max}
· Transition rate: |\dot\lambda|\le\dot\lambda_{\max}

6.2 ECBF for Gap Confinement

Define h=g-g_{\min}. The gap dynamics take the form:

\ddot g=f_g(x)+g_g(x)F_{\rm active}

Then the ECBF condition is:

\boxed{
L_f^2h+L_gL_fh\,F_{\rm active}+K_1L_fh+K_0h\ge 0
}

with K_1=2\zeta\omega_n, K_0=\omega_n^2. For \omega_n=62.8 rad/s, \zeta=0.7: K_1\approx 88, K_0\approx 3944.

Upper gap: \bar h=g_{\max}-g, same structure.

6.3 CBF for Wheel-Load Positivity

h_W=F_{W,i}-F_{W,\min},\qquad \dot h_W+\alpha(h_W)\ge 0

Relative degree 1 with respect to suspension force.

6.4 CBF for Power Dissipation

h_D=P_{\max}-P_D(v,g)\ge 0

The derivative is:

\dot P_D
=
\frac{\partial P_D}{\partial v}\dot v
+
\frac{\partial P_D}{\partial g}\dot g

Both \dot v (controlled by propulsion) and \dot g (controlled by active suspension) appear. The control input is therefore:

u=
\begin{bmatrix}
u_{\rm thrust}\\
u_{\rm active}
\end{bmatrix}

and the CBF is relative degree 1 with respect to this combined input.

6.5 CBF for True Transition Rate

Define:

h_\lambda^+=\dot\lambda_{\max}-\dot\lambda\ge 0,\qquad h_\lambda^-=\dot\lambda_{\max}+\dot\lambda\ge 0

with \dot\lambda given by Lemma 1. Both are relative degree 1 with respect to \dot F_{\rm active}. Enforce via:

\dot h_\lambda^\pm+\alpha(h_\lambda^\pm)\ge 0

6.6 QP Formulation

\min_{\mathbf{F}}\|\mathbf{F}-\mathbf{F}_{\rm nom}\|^2

subject to ECBF gap, CBF wheel, CBF power, CBF transition rate, actuator limits.

