7. Fault Tolerance

7.1 Wheel-Supported Target Set

\mathcal{C}_{\rm wheel}=\left\{
x:
\begin{aligned}
&g_i\le g_{\rm contact}\\
&F_{W,i}\ge F_{W,\min}\\
&|\dot F_{W,i}|\le\dot F_{W,\max}\\
&|\ddot z|\le a_{z,\max}\\
&J_{\rm landing}\le J_{\rm absorbable}
\end{aligned}
\right\}

J_{\rm landing}=\frac12 m\dot z^2+\frac12 I_\theta\dot\theta^2+\frac12 I_\phi\dot\phi^2

7.2 Admissibility and Falsification

\boxed{
\forall f\in\mathcal{F}_{\rm admissible},\;x_0\in\mathcal{K}_{\rm operating}\Rightarrow x_0\in\operatorname{Capt}(\mathcal{K},\mathcal{C}_{\rm wheel})
}

Falsified if \exists x_0\in\mathcal{K}_{\rm operating} with x_0\notin\operatorname{Capt}(\mathcal{K},\mathcal{C}_{\rm wheel}).

7.3 Capture Basin Definition

\operatorname{Capt}(\mathcal{K},\mathcal{C})=\left\{x_0\in\mathcal{K}:\exists u(\cdot),\exists T\ge 0,\;x(t)\in\mathcal{K}\;\forall t\in[0,T],\;x(T)\in\mathcal{C}\right\}

7.4 CLF Sufficient Condition

If there exists V(x) and invariant \Omega\subset\mathcal{K} with \dot V\le-\alpha V+\beta\|d\|, and \Omega\subseteq\operatorname{Capt}(\mathcal{K},\mathcal{C}_{\rm wheel}), then admissibility holds on \Omega.

