8. Corridor Network

8.1 Hybrid Graph

\boxed{
G=(V,E_0\cup E_M)
}

where E_0 are ordinary asphalt edges (\lambda=0) and E_M are magnetic-corridor edges (transition permitted).

8.2 Edge Transitions

· On E_0: Mode 0 or Mode 3.
· On E_M with v\ge v_{\rm engage}: transition to Mode 1, then Mode 2.
· On E_M with v<v_{\rm engage}: Mode 0 or Mode 1 partial.
· Entering E_0 from E_M: forced transition to Mode 0 or 3.

8.3 Route Planning

For a route P=(e_1,\dots,e_n), the vehicle must choose engagement and disengagement points, respecting:

v_{\rm engage}>v_{\rm phys},\qquad v_{\rm disengage}<v_{\rm phys}

This is a hybrid optimal control problem on G.

