Appendix F: Lateral Guidance Architecture

F.1 Inherent Lateral Instability

Proposition F.1. A Halbach array over a uniform conductive sheet has zero lateral force at centered position and non-positive lateral stiffness:

\frac{\partial F_y^{\rm lateral}}{\partial y}\le0

Vertical PMEDS lift alone does not guarantee lateral stability.

F.2 Passive Perforated Guideway

Recent experimental work has proposed a passive self-centering perforated guideway featuring periodic symmetric rectangular apertures that reshape eddy currents into an electromagnetic potential well. This produces a lateral restoring force without auxiliary magnets or coils:

\boxed{
F_y^{\rm passive}=F_y^{\rm passive}(y),\qquad
\frac{\partial F_y^{\rm passive}}{\partial y}<0
}

The mechanism has been validated through 3D theoretical models, periodic lateral–longitudinal simulations, multi-objective optimization, and physical guideway tests.

F.3 Active Correction Layer

Control coils with bandwidth \ge100 Hz provide correction for large perturbations, asymmetric loading, and transients exceeding passive authority:

\boxed{
F_y^{\rm active}=F_y^{\rm active}(u_y)
}

F.4 Combined Lateral Stiffness

\boxed{
k_y^{\rm total}=k_y^{\rm passive}+k_y^{\rm active}
}

The passive layer dominates for small perturbations; the active layer dominates for large perturbations.

F.5 Lateral Force Decomposition

F_y^{\rm lateral}=F_y^{\rm passive}+F_y^{\rm geometry}+F_y^{\rm active}

where F_y^{\rm geometry} accounts for finite-width and edge effects of the conductive track.

---

Appendix G: Actuator Dynamics and Bidirectional Force

G.1 First-Order Actuator Model

The active correction force is governed by:

\boxed{
\tau_F\dot F_{\rm active}=-F_{\rm active}+F_{\rm cmd}
}

with time constant \tau_F determined by actuator bandwidth.

G.2 Bidirectional Force Limits

F_{\rm active}\in[-F_{\rm active,max}^-,\;F_{\rm active,max}^+]

The negative limit F_{\rm active,max}^- must be physically realized by the actuator architecture. This requires a mechanical reaction path between the vehicle body and the magnetic subsystem, allowing the actuator to pull downward when passive lift exceeds mg.

G.3 Steady-State Force

At equilibrium:

F_{\rm active}=F_{\rm cmd}

The equilibrium manifold is:

\mathcal{E}_{\rm hybrid}=\{(v,g,F_{\rm active}):F_{\rm PMEDS}(v,g)+F_{\rm active}=mg\}

G.4 Separation from Passive Manifold

The true passive equilibrium manifold:

\mathcal{E}_{\rm passive}=\{(v,g):F_{\rm PMEDS}(v,g)=mg\}

is a subset of \mathcal{E}_{\rm hybrid} corresponding to F_{\rm active}=0.

